    <briefdescription>
<para>No-op feature flag provider — all flags are always disabled. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Use in unit tests or builds where feature-flag evaluation is not needed. <ref refid="classthemis_1_1core_1_1concerns_1_1_no_op_feature_flags_1a384ddbbfb1638e6cb2745502d9db29eb" kindref="member">setValue()</ref> is intentionally ignored and does not persist any state. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
